<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haute-Garonne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haute-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in the Occitanie region, stretching from the Spanish border in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> along the upper Garonne to the plain around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, its prefecture. Created in 1790, it includes the historic district of Comminges, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugdunum-convenarum">Saint-Bertrand-de-Comminges</a> and Saint-Gaudens.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haute-garonne.jpg" alt="Haute-Garonne" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pistolero31 from Vers Paris · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toulouse_-_Le_clocher_de_la_cath%C3%A9drale_depuis_la_cour_de_la_pr%C3%A9fecture_(14925567135).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
